          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ham zadan pairs ham, \"together\", with zadan, \"to strike\": to beat together. ham is inherited: EtymDB traces it to Middle Persian ham and Old Persian hama-, \"same, together\". zadan, \"to strike\", is an inherited verb; it is usually traced to Middle Persian zadan."
            }
          ]
        },
